Scope confirmed via `git diff master --stat` in the snapshot: GV3 touched
web/templates/components/whatif/guardrail_optimizer.html (+25/-? lines),
internal/handlers/whatif/handlers_guardrail_optimizer.go, handlers.go,
internal/models/whatif.go, plus tests. web/static/css/styles.css,
projection-chart.html, engine/month.go, engine/stepper.go, htmx.min.js are
GV2/vendor changes in the same tree — excluded from this verdict, noted as
OBSERVATION only per instructions.

Method: cp -a snapshot at /tmp/budget2-gv3-snap (kept .git). Server started
isolated via `scripts/whatif-verify.sh start 8093` (own data/backups copy,
LIVE data never written), stopped cleanly at the end
(`scripts/whatif-verify.sh stop 8093`). Real server render only — no
hand-built HTML. Playwright (npx-cached `playwright` 1.63.0 module) +
axe-core 4.13.0 (from the globally-installed @axe-core/cli package) driving
Chrome 152 (/opt/google/chrome/chrome). Screenshots and axe JSON under
/tmp/budget2-gv3-snap/a11y-out/.

A-1 Automated audit (npx @axe-core/cli-equivalent axe.run, tags
wcag2a/wcag2aa/wcag21a/wcag21aa/wcag22aa):
  - axe-light-before (CLI, /whatif before running optimizer): 0 violations
    (a11y-out/axe-light-before/, log in audit.log)
  - light-before (Playwright+axe, pre-optimizer): 0 violations, 1 incomplete
    (color-contrast on Plotly SVG axis-title text — projection chart, GV2
    scope, pre-existing bgOverlap axe limitation, not a GV3 surface)
  - dark-before: 0 violations, 1 incomplete (same Plotly cause)
  - light-after (optimizer run + results rendered): 0 violations, 1
    incomplete (color-contrast "incomplete" on site-nav `.md:text-2xl` /
    nav links — header nav from base.html, byte-identical to master, NOT
    touched by GV3; confirmed via `git diff master --stat` showing
    base.html absent from the changed-file list)
  - dark-after: 0 violations, 1 incomplete (same nav cause)
  - axe-dump-light / axe-dump-dark (isolated real-template render, see
    below): 0 violations, 0 incomplete — the cleanest evidence, since it
    isolates the GV3 partial from the pre-existing nav/chart noise.
  Full JSON: a11y-out/axe-{light,dark}-{before,after}.json,
  a11y-out/axe-dump-{light,dark}.json.

  To reach every GV3 wording surface (plan-floor notice, the plan-design
  "Below target — planned spending is below your minimum from year N" row
  wording, and the 100.00% worst-annual-cut saturation explanation) I wrote
  a throwaway Go test,
  internal/handlers/whatif/zzgv3_a11y_dump_test.go (deleted after the run,
  never committed), that calls the SAME renderer.RenderPartial the real
  handler uses on "whatif-guardrail-optimizer" and
  "whatif-guardrail-optimizer-results" with a fixture combining: a
  PlanFloor notice, one Qualifies row, one PlanDesignBelowTarget row, and
  one P95WorstAnnualCutPct=100.0 row (mirrors the pattern in the worker's
  own guardrail_plan_floor_test.go, `renderer.RenderPartial` call at line
  150). Output dumped to /tmp/budget2-gv3-a11y-dump.html, then wrapped in
  <html class=""> / <html class="dark"> pages loading the REAL, currently
  running server's built stylesheets (http://localhost:8093/static/css/
  tailwind.css and styles.css) — a11y-out/dump-light.html,
  dump-dark.html, screenshots dump-light.png / dump-dark.png. This is a
  real server-render byte source (html/template execution), not
  hand-built markup or guessed CSS. I also confirmed the real backend
  reaches the plan-design row wording live (no synthetic data needed for
  that one): POST /whatif/guardrails/optimize with floor=7500/8500 against
  the isolated data copy returned "Below target — planned spending is
  below your minimum from year 18" for the Current-guardrails /
  Guardrails-disabled baselines (/tmp/opt-response.html,
  /tmp/opt-response2.html) — real requests take 41–70s each (curl -w
  time_total), which is why I raised the Playwright timeouts to 150s (the
  task's "15-30s" estimate was short for this environment; verified with a
  raw curl POST timing first before trusting any Playwright timeout).

A-2 Both themes: light and dark audited at every stage above via
  playwright colorScheme context (`prefers-color-scheme` toggle, matches
  the site's own base.html media-query default-theme logic — no
  localStorage override needed since neither test set one) and via the
  `dark` class on <html> for the isolated dump. Screenshots:
  a11y-out/light-before.png, dark-before.png, light-after.png,
  dark-after.png, dump-light.png, dump-dark.png.

A-3 Contrast — computed from actual getComputedStyle() color/
  backgroundColor pairs captured by Playwright (WCAG relative-luminance
  formula, python3 script inline above):
  LIGHT: hint/plan-floor form note (text-gray-600 on white) 7.63:1;
    results notice (text-warning #92400e on bg-warning-soft #fffbeb)
    6.84:1; row wording / 100% explanation (plain body text, no color
    override — text-gray-900-ish on white) 17.49:1.
  DARK: hint/plan-floor form note (dark:text-gray-300 on gray-900)
    11.74:1; results notice (text-warning #fbbf24 on bg-warning-soft-dark
    #261e22) 9.74:1; row wording / 100% explanation (dark body text on
    gray-900) 16.03:1.
  All ratios exceed the 4.5:1 AA body-text threshold in both themes with
  wide margin. Source: a11y-out/dump_audit.log.

A-4/A-5 Keyboard + visible focus:
  - Floor field aria-describedby (live server, plan-floor fixture already
    present in the shipped data): "guardrail-optimizer-floor-help
    guardrail-optimizer-status guardrail-optimizer-floor-plan-note";
    describedbyText resolved all three ids to real paragraph text
    including the new plan-floor hint (a11y-out/audit.log, "FLOOR
    aria-describedby:" line). ARIA snapshot of the field:
    `- spinbutton "Minimum monthly living spending (today's dollars,
    required)": "7500"` (a11y-out/floor-field-axtree.txt) — accessible
    name/value correct; the description is not part of ariaSnapshot's
    terse output but is independently confirmed by the id-resolution dump
    above, which is the load-bearing check per A-4.
  - Field is keyboard-focusable (page.locator(...).focus() +
    activeElement.id check, both true).
  - Visible focus ring measured via getComputedStyle: light
    outline:"rgb(79,70,229) solid 2px" + matching box-shadow; dark
    outline:"rgb(165,180,252) solid 2px" — both well over 3:1 against
    their background (indigo-600 on white; indigo-300 on gray-900).
  - After the real optimizer run, focus lands on the outcome <h4
    data-guardrail-outcome tabindex="-1">: confirmed with a dedicated
    check (a11y-out/focus_check.cjs) — `document.activeElement === outcome`
    is true, activeTag "H4", activeText "No options met your
    minimum-spending target" (the element carries no `id`, so the
    id-based check in the main audit script printed an empty string —
    a harness false-negative, not a real defect; corrected with the
    element-identity check). No keyboard trap observed in either flow.

A-6 Structure: H1 count = 1 (a11y-out/audit.log "H1 count: 1", full-page
  check). Heading order in the optimizer surface: h3 "Optimize
  guardrails" -> h4 "Options meet your minimum-spending target" (outcome)
  -> h4 (empty, #guardrail-graph-heading inside the `hidden`
  #guardrail-graph-preview panel — GV2 scope, unpopulated/hidden until a
  graph loads, so not exposed to AT; confirmed via source at
  a11y-out/dump-light.html line ~259). No skipped levels. The plan-floor
  notice renders as `<p data-guardrail-plan-floor-notice>` (confirmed in
  rendered HTML), not a heading — matches spec.

A-7 Table: `<table>` with `<th scope="col">` for all 5 columns (Policy /
  Chance of maintaining minimum / Lifetime living spending (median) /
  Worst annual cut / Actions) — unchanged by GV3's diff (only `<td>`
  cell content changed).

A-8 Icons: no new icons in the GV3 diff (text-only additions); N/A.

A-9 Never color-only: the plan-design "Below target" wording carries its
  full meaning in text ("Below target — planned spending is below your
  minimum from year N", verified live: /tmp/opt-response.html rows) not
  via color alone; the notice's text-warning/bg-warning-soft styling is
  accompanied by full explanatory sentences, not a bare color cue; the
  100.00% cell's saturation explanation is plain appended text, same body
  color as the rest of the cell (no color-only signal).

A-10 Live updates: #guardrail-optimizer-status has role="status"
  aria-live="polite". After a real optimizer run its textContent equals
  the outcome heading text + " " + the plan-floor-notice text, joined
  once (a11y-out/audit.log "STATUS REGION:" — statusText exactly equals
  `outcomeText + ' ' + noticeText`), matching the GV3 script's single
  `status.textContent=...` assignment (guardrail_optimizer.html diff, the
  `outcomeText=[outcome?.textContent.trim(),planFloorNotice?.textContent
  .trim()].filter(Boolean).join(' ')` line) — one assignment, one
  announcement, not two. Focus moves to the outcome heading as
  established under A-4/A-5, preserving the "focus/scroll preserved"
  half of A-10 (this endpoint is a fetch+innerHTML swap, not the SSE
  refresh A-10 primarily targets, but the same single-update contract
  holds).
  OBSERVATION (pre-existing, not GV3): the visible #guardrail-optimizer-
  status paragraph duplicates the outcome heading's text on screen (once
  in the status line, once as the h4 below) — this pattern predates GV3
  (the status paragraph already echoed the outcome text before this task;
  GV3 only appended the notice text into that same single assignment).
  Not a WCAG failure (a status message repeating subsequent visible
  content is not itself a criterion violation), but flagged for the
  backlog as a possible future de-dup.

