Reflow: at both 1024px and 375px viewports, document.documentElement.
  scrollWidth === clientWidth (no page-level horizontal scroll) —
  a11y-out/audit.log "Reflow @1024px:... horizontalOverflow=false",
  "Reflow @375px:... horizontalOverflow=false". The table's own
  `role="region"` scroll container (aria-label "Guardrail comparison;
  scroll horizontally for all measures", tabindex="0") legitimately
  overflows internally at 375px (scrollWidth 529 vs clientWidth 299,
  a11y-out/crop_375.cjs output) — that is its documented, intended
  behavior, not a page-reflow defect. Cropped screenshot:
  a11y-out/optimizer-section-375.png confirms readable text and no
  clipped content at narrow width.

